# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What belongs in this repository: the five skills, the two workbench templates,
# the audit tooling, TEAM.md and the eval cases. Everything else is either
# generated, installed from elsewhere, or working notes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies and build output — the workbench templates ship a package.json and
# a lockfile, never an installed tree.
node_modules/
dist/
.output/
.astro/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.vite/

# Logs
*.log

# Working documents. The plan and the decisions log are how this was built, not
# what it is. Their conclusions live in TEAM.md and inside the skills themselves.
PLAN-*.md
NOTES-*.md

# Skills installed here to work with, not authored here — including the copies
# ui-kickoff puts inside a workbench. The `**/` matters: a pattern with a slash
# in the middle is anchored to this file's directory, so a bare `.claude/skills/`
# would cover the root and quietly miss `design/.claude/skills/`.
**/.claude/skills/
**/.github/skills/
**/.cursor/skills/
**/.gemini/skills/

# Copilot slash commands, installed the same way. The source is assets/prompts/,
# which is what the package ships and what the installer copies from.
.github/prompts/

# Local agent settings. Note that `.claude/settings.json` is NOT ignored: the
# permission rules it carries are project facts and belong in the repository.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# In THIS repository only. `design/.ui/` is a vendored copy of
# skills/ui-composition/scripts/, which lives ten lines away in the same tree.
# In a client project it is the only copy of the tooling and MUST be committed —
# ui-kickoff puts it there for exactly that reason.
design/.ui/

# The tarball `npm pack` leaves behind. The package is published, not committed.
*.tgz

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because each one is shared state somebody depends on:
#   package-lock.json    the pin that makes "it built in March" and
#                        "it builds in September" the same sentence
#   .promoted.json       promotion stamps — the state ui-drift compares against,
#                        shared between designers and developers
#   ui-audit.config.json per-project budgets and overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
